# Top-level Python dependencies of PIE's imaging stack: pie/imaging, the pie/stats and modelling code its tests
# import, and FastSurfer, which runs in this same environment (pie.imaging.fastsurfer's PIE_FASTSURFER_PYTHON).
# Compiled to requirements-imaging.lock (CUDA 12.8) and requirements-imaging-cpu.lock (CPU: CI, GPU-less enclaves).
# Versions are pinned there, not here. Regenerate with the command in each lock's header (uv 0.7+); uv keeps the pins
# already in the -o file, so adding a package does not move the others. The locks were first pinned to venv_imaging
# as of 11 Oct 2026 (pandas 3.0.3, torch 2.7.1+cu128) by adding
#   -c <(venv_imaging/bin/python -m pip freeze --exclude-editable | grep -v ' @ ' | sed -E 's/\+cu[0-9]+$//')
# to that command; do the same to re-pin from a changed venv. Install: uv pip sync --torch-backend cu128 (or cpu) <lock>.

# FastSurfer 2.6.0-dev0 (Deep-MI/FastSurfer@d0d7d39, the snapshot PIE's T1 validation ran on): its pyproject
# dependencies plus the qc/lit extras its requirements.txt installs
